<title>USA: Heinz cutting 2,500 jobs, closing 25 plants.</title>
<headline>Heinz cutting 2,500 jobs, closing 25 plants.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>H.J. Heinz Co. announced a major restructuring Friday, saying it will close or sell at least 25 plants, cut 2,500 jobs worldwide and take a $650 million pre-tax charge this year to cover the costs.</p>
<p>The company, which produces a wide variety of food products besides its famous condiments, said it expected the measures to result in pre-tax savings of about $120 million next year.</p>
<p>The Pittsburgh-based global food marketer told a financial analysts meeting in San Francisco that it will exit at least four &quot;non-strategic&quot; businesses as part of the reorganization, the biggest in its history.</p>
<p>Heinz's stock added 75 cents to $42.50 in early afternoon trading on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
